module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.one_value_two_renderings_compared_for_equality

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data one_value_two_renderings_compared_for_equality: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "one_value_two_renderings_compared_for_equality" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**two RENDERINGS of one value are compared for equality, and both renderings are correct** (INVALID STATE: a digest, id, key or handle is produced on one side of a comparison by one function and on the other side by a different function, and the two functions disagree about how the value is SPELLED -- a prefix, a case, a separator, a unit suffix, a zero-pad. Neither spelling is wrong: each is a faithful rendering of the same underlying value, and each is correct where it was written. The defect is that the comparison was written between the two RENDERERS rather than downstream of one. HARM: the comparison can never hold. Where it guards a wall, the wall refuses unconditionally and the refusal names a real-sounding cause it did not measure; where it selects a cached or matching element, nothing ever matches and the expensive arm always runs. ",

    "Recognition rule, and it is mechanical: at any comparison over an identity-like value, ask whether BOTH SIDES WERE PRODUCED BY THE SAME RENDERER. If the two sides trace back to two functions, the comparison is between spellings, not values, and the spellings are a second place the representation is decided -- §3's nickname defect one level down, at the VALUE layer rather than the name layer. The repair is at the source: one renderer, both sides. A comparison that normalizes -- strips the prefix, lowercases, trims -- is not the repair, it is a THIRD place the spelling is decided, and it is how this class gets rebuilt the next time a producer is added. ",

    "THE REACHABILITY HALF IS WHY IT SURVIVES, AND IT BELONGS IN THE ROW. This class hides behind arms that the common case does not reach. A gate whose failing comparison is evaluated only on a rare path -- a second generation, a retry, a cache miss, a conflict -- is PERMANENTLY GREEN on every ordinary run, and that green reads as coverage. So the discriminating control cannot be an ordinary run: it must DRIVE THE RARE CASE, and a control that passes without reaching the arm proves nothing about it. This is the same shape as a_superset_check_is_a_candidate_list, asked at the level of reachability rather than of precision. ",

    "TESTS AROUND IT ARE STRUCTURALLY BLIND WHEN THEY INJECT THE PRODUCER. The specimen's convergence tests supply the digest producer as a closure returning a literal -- `|| Ok(\"seed-2\".to_string())` -- so both sides of the comparison are the injected spelling and agree trivially. Injecting a producer to make a test hermetic also removes the RENDERING from the test's subject, so the one thing this class lives in is the one thing those tests cannot see. A control for this class must run the real renderers. ",

    "SPECIMEN, measured by execution rather than read (gunbc, 2026-09-07, silent-otter-161). `claim_executor --regen-round-cost` refused with `CandidateGeneratedByDifferentSeed: stage admitted executable 6ecf9df3571be528 but next generation would run fnv1a64:6ecf9df3571be528` -- the refusal PRINTED BOTH SIDES and they carry the same hex. In `v1_compiler.required_regen_host`, `current_exe_digest` and `next_pass_executable_digest` rendered the seed executable's digest BARE via `v1_rt::bytes_identity_hash`, while `path_digest` rendered it through `bytes_digest`, which formats the hash under an `fnv1a64:` prefix; `run_built_seed_regen` compared the two with `!=`. The arm is reached only on GENERATION 2 of a convergence round -- that is, only when a round actually has drift to INSTALL -- so every no-drift round reported `first_generation_equal=true`, never entered it, and stayed green. The consequence is the one worth teaching: for as long as the defect stood, every round that needed an install refused and restored its checkpoint, so the sanctioned install route was dead for exactly the case it exists for, and the lanes that needed it got a restore instead of an install. ",

    "WHAT THE NEIGHBOURING ROWS DO NOT COVER, checked before this row was filed. `comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares` is the projection shape: there the key is a COMPONENT of the identity and the harm is that two distinct elements collide under one key -- a wrong answer about the right value. Here both sides carry the WHOLE value and nothing collides; the harm is that equal values compare unequal. `surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity` is the nearest neighbour and is genuinely adjacent, being about representation rather than components, but there a surface spelling is consumed WHERE A RESOLVED BINDING WAS AVAILABLE and the harm is a wrongly constructed value; here both spellings are resolved, correct, and constructed rightly. `refusal_names_a_comparison_and_prints_neither_side` is this row's mirror: that class hides the operands, and this specimen printed them -- which is exactly how it was caught in one read. `subject_and_its_digest_as_independent_parameters` is about a digest travelling separately from what it digests; here one subject was digested twice. ",

    "Next-rung trigger, named as the capability rather than as an artifact: a rendered identity is carried as a TYPE whose construction admits one rendering, so a second spelling has no constructor and a comparison between two renderers cannot be written. Until that exists, the class is mechanically preventable at best -- one renderer per value by review, plus a control that reaches the rare arm -- and a per-site normalization is a regression, not a repair.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
